WEBVTT

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:20.310
Roughly ten years ago,
the Demon Lord's Domain appeared,

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:23.350
and mankind had their territory
taken from them.

00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:25.020
The Gran Chaos Empire put forward

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.520
the Declaration of Mankind's Common
Front Against the Demon Race,

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.280
or "Mankind Declaration" for short.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.320
Nations that signed on to
the Mankind Declaration

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.740
ratified the following three articles.

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:39.200
The first article states that changes
in borders among mankind

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:42.790
due to military action are not recognized.

00:00:42.790 --> 00:00:45.290
The Principality of Amidonia
signed this treaty,

00:00:45.290 --> 00:00:48.130
while the Kingdom of Elfrieden
did not sign.

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:51.800
Thus, when the Principality of
Amidonia lost their capital, Van,

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:55.550
it was possible under Article 1 for them
to appeal to the Gran Chaos Empire,

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:58.550
the power behind the Mankind Declaration,

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:00.970
for the right to the return
of their territory.

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:04.560
<i>"...Keep on going anyway"</i>

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:13.610
<i>Our bond strikes deep into my left breast</i>

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:22.450
<i>We enjoy a fleeting happiness</i>
<i>after weathering one fog,</i>

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:27.460
<i>until our vision becomes obscured again</i>

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:33.420
<i>Bitterly betrayed, we grow</i>
<i>disgusted by our destiny</i>

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:38.300
<i>But why does the dawn still come?</i>

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:43.640
<i>We close our eyes and try to remember</i>

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:48.980
<i>the chance of stopping, of never meeting</i>

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:54.570
<i>From boundless zero to infinity,</i>

00:01:54.570 --> 00:02:00.070
<i>dreaming is the heartbeat of believing</i>

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:03.910
<i>We'll move along alone and in pairs</i>

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:10.040
<i>Don't stay put; our small,</i>
<i>though by no means helpless steps</i>

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:14.840
<i>will open uncharted territory</i>
<i>for each of us</i>

00:02:14.840 --> 00:02:20.930
<i>Realize we will never again</i>
<i>let our dreams die on the vine</i>

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:27.730
<i>The tear tracks that run down</i>
<i>our cheeks are shooting stars</i>

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:31.560
<i>We're going to grab hold of them</i>

00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:35.070
"Becoming Good Friends Who Never Offend"

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:45.830
Diplomacy between the Gran Chaos Empire
and the Kingdom of Elfrieden

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:47.620
is back in session.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:48.870
Yeah.

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:55.460
Thank you for the meal.

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:57.380
It was quite delicious.

00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:02.590
Ordinarily, we would have
held a banquet for you.

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:05.310
I will thank you for your food in kind.

00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:09.060
Allow me to provide you with a tidbit
of information I had been saving--

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:10.730
monster meat.

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:11.940
Huh?

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:17.230
The meat from monsters can be eaten.

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:23.030
For real? By "monsters," you mean the
ones from the Demon Lord's Domain?

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:26.280
Yes. Their flavor is surprisingly normal.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.330
Jeanne, you've eaten it yourself?!

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:32.000
She has such a cute face,
but she's surprisingly wild.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.380
It wasn't kobold meat,
by any chance, was it?

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:41.010
It was <i>monster </i>meat that I ate.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:45.050
I would never dream of eating
the more person-like <i>demons</i>.

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:49.100
Yeah, well, I can't really tell
the difference between the two.

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:53.480
Ah, that's right, you are a
summoned hero, aren't you?

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.730
Do you know about our punitive action?

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:59.530
Yes, I heard about it from
the former King Albert.

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:01.990
It was ten years ago now,

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:06.280
but our punitive force was
wiped out by the demons.

00:04:06.280 --> 00:04:09.740
When my sister was nine, and I was seven,

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:13.580
the punitive force was led
by the previous emperor...

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:16.790
...which is to say, our father.

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:18.800
I heard that when they were
attacked by the monsters,

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:22.300
a horrific scene of cruelty played out.

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:25.340
The flames spat by the monsters
turned cities into scorched earth,

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:29.720
and people were killed and devoured
without regard to age or gender.

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:32.060
They were only running
rampant on instinct,

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:35.150
so some people managed
to get away from them.

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:37.730
They sound like wild animals.

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:41.360
Meanwhile, the demons demonstrated
well-organized behavior,

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:45.030
beating our punitive force
with overwhelming strength.

00:04:45.030 --> 00:04:47.200
Their circumstances
after being beaten varied,

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.660
with some saying that they were not
pursued as they retreated,

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:55.580
while others said that raping, pillaging,
and butchery all took place.

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:59.210
Almost as though you were facing
other people as opponents.

00:04:59.210 --> 00:05:01.590
Where does the difference arise?

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:04.720
Did demons evolve out of monsters?

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:08.680
They gained their intelligence
by eating people's brains.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:12.560
At least, that's what the religious
folks made a fuss about for a time.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:14.230
But that story was full of holes.

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:19.110
Be that as it may, since our
battle lines became entrenched,

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:22.570
the monsters are the only ones
who have been attacking.

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:27.990
Which is why it can be said that we
have the current situation in hand.

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:32.700
We kind of got way off the subject of
being able to eat monsters, didn't we?

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:36.620
What I ate was the meat
of a giant winged serpent.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:38.920
A winged snake?

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:43.670
It was a giant snake with four
bird-like wings growing out of it.

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:48.970
As I recall, Central and South America
had a god named Quetzalcoatl.

00:05:48.970 --> 00:05:51.810
I don't know what possessed you
to want to eat something like that.

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:56.890
It tasted like a regular snake.
It was closer to bird than it was fish.

00:05:56.890 --> 00:06:02.480
"It tasted like a regular snake"?
Then she's eaten snake before?

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:07.860
Jeanne, for a princess, you certainly
have eaten some unusual things.

00:06:07.860 --> 00:06:10.780
I'm also a general leading troops.

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:14.660
In times of need,
we will eat whatever we can.

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:16.580
I suppose that's reasonable.

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:20.960
But ordinarily, you wouldn't go out
of your way to try monster, right?

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:25.670
One of our scout parties discovered
the remains of cooked monsters.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:28.590
So are you saying...?

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:33.810
We believe the demons ate the monsters.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:39.690
So, when we had the chance to capture
a monster of the same species,

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:42.730
we verified whether
or not they were edible.

00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:47.280
Upon trying it, I found its taste
to be light, yet refreshing.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:51.280
Whoa, there's something I'm far more
interested in than just the flavor.

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:52.740
There is?

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:57.160
The fact that demons were eating
monsters is much more shocking.

00:06:57.160 --> 00:07:02.290
Meaning that demons don't regard
monsters as their equals, do they?

00:07:04.540 --> 00:07:06.130
Tell me, Jeanne...

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:07.590
What is it?

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:12.890
Could demons and monsters be the same
as what we call people and animals?

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:18.270
What makes you think that?

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:24.060
Liscia, could you stop
taking notes for a moment?

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:25.730
All right.

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:29.240
This must be disturbing if you don't
want to leave a public record of it.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:32.280
I can't wait to hear what kind of
bombshell you're about to drop.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:35.240
Forgive me, I realize
that in some situations,

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:38.120
these might be taken as
discriminatory remarks, so...

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:43.630
Discriminatory remarks? You mean,
regarding monsters and demons?

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:50.300
In my eyes, I can't differentiate between
this world's animals and monsters.

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:53.890
The rest of you probably can't
imagine how that feels, can you?

00:07:53.890 --> 00:07:58.010
More to the point,
I have trouble telling the difference

00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:00.560
between races like beastmen
and dragonewts, and demons.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:03.140
Wha--? That's...

00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:07.190
I grew up in a world where we
had no beastmen or demons,

00:08:07.190 --> 00:08:09.070
so I don't understand
how they're different.

00:08:09.070 --> 00:08:10.400
Well for starters, demons are--

00:08:10.400 --> 00:08:12.200
You can't tell when you look at Tomoe?!

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:15.950
Your Majesty! To say that goes
too far is an understatement!

00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:17.490
Like I said!

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:21.330
Like I said, this could end up
being taken as discriminatory!

00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:28.550
Jeanne, can you tell the difference
between mystic wolves,

00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:30.670
mystic foxes, and kobolds?

00:08:30.670 --> 00:08:34.550
Of course I can.
Kobolds have dog-like faces.

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:39.600
But there are also races of beastmen
who have animal-like faces, right?

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:43.180
Now that you mention it, I suppose so.

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:48.060
Ah, I know! Kobolds have
bodies that are covered in fur.

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:51.280
If that's the case, then how
can you tell apart a demon

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:53.700
who has no fur, or even short fur?

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:02.250
Now that you point it out,
for the first time,

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:04.960
I realize that I've been differentiating
between people and demons

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:06.500
based on my senses alone.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:09.340
You're right. When you put it that way,

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:11.630
I can't think of a single thing
that sets them apart.

00:09:11.630 --> 00:09:14.760
How is it that we never noticed before?

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:19.930
It's probably a shared
awareness in this world.

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:21.850
They have a sensate understanding
of the difference

00:09:21.850 --> 00:09:24.230
between mankind and demon.

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:27.230
I'm glad you said this was not
to be mentioned to anyone.

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:31.940
If any bureaucrats had been in here,
we may have had to slay them.

00:09:31.940 --> 00:09:35.780
Huh?! Y-You'd go that far
over something like this?!

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:37.610
Yes, I would.

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:42.700
If word of this got out,
the supercontinent could erupt in riots.

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:44.370
Isn't that right, Hakuya?

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:46.080
You are correct.

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:48.830
If the idea that demons and
beastmen are not all that different

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:51.130
were to become widespread,

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:53.210
then countries like the
Principality of Amidonia,

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:55.050
which are human supremacists,

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:58.390
or races that do not recognize
multiracial people, like the high elves,

00:09:58.390 --> 00:10:02.350
will end up being given just what
they need to start launching attacks.

00:10:03.890 --> 00:10:08.690
It could mean beastmen and dragonewts
being ostracized as demons,

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:11.650
and becoming the targets of oppression.

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:20.700
It would also spark interracial strife
within our respective countries.

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:24.490
I'm sorry. I hadn't thought it
through that far.

00:10:24.490 --> 00:10:25.910
Not at all.

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:29.210
It's better than having it thrust
upon us all of a sudden one day.

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:31.920
I'm glad to hear you say that.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:35.510
On the other hand, I can't
think of a way to counter it.

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:39.050
If we think of demons
as being an ethnic minority,

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:43.390
the Mankind Declaration does make
an appeal against persecuting minorities.

00:10:43.390 --> 00:10:44.680
But...

00:10:44.680 --> 00:10:50.600
...that agreement is between states.
It has no bearing on the general public.

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:54.440
At most, we could inquire of a nation
about their supervisory responsibilities.

00:10:54.440 --> 00:10:57.280
For that matter, there are
also nations, such as ours,

00:10:57.280 --> 00:11:00.320
which are not signatories
to the Mankind Declaration.

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:03.320
If a foreign power were to force
their policy upon them,

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:06.870
there would be a backlash,
and in the worst case, start a war.

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:10.330
That is correct. And it isn't as though
we have all the information there is

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:13.170
about monsters and demons anyway.

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:17.960
With so many unknowns,
leaping to any conclusions is dangerous.

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:23.050
All right.

00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:29.390
How about the empire and the kingdom
continue to discuss this matter further?

00:11:29.390 --> 00:11:31.060
Agreed.

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:43.910
Well, it's time we started
discussing the occupation of Van.

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:47.290
In accordance with
the Mankind Declaration,

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:51.210
the empire cannot recognize the
altering of borders by military force.

00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:55.000
And the kingdom cannot comply
with your request to return the land.

00:11:55.000 --> 00:11:57.920
Amidonia was the one
who started all of this.

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:00.050
If you allow this kind of outrage,

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:02.380
you will lose the respect

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:05.010
of both Mankind Declaration member
and non-member nations.

00:12:05.010 --> 00:12:09.850
You may be right. Which is why
the empire will likely end up

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:13.650
having Amidonia pay
commensurate reparations.

00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:16.650
And if we don't accept,
will you resort to armed force?

00:12:16.650 --> 00:12:18.570
If it becomes necessary.

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:24.410
With the forces I currently
have stationed nearby,

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:26.370
I am confident that I could wipe out

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:29.330
both the kingdom's forces and the
principality's forces at the same time.

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:31.000
I'll bet you could.

00:12:31.000 --> 00:12:33.670
For our part, we do not wish to fight.

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:37.210
So let's first lay out
both of our intentions.

00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:41.380
The empire does not wish to
recognize the change in borders.

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:46.390
That is why you want Van returned.
That much is correct, right?

00:12:46.390 --> 00:12:48.970
Yes, that is correct.

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:52.140
My kingdom wishes to curb
the Principality of Amidonia's ability

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:55.190
to keep taking hostile actions toward us.

00:12:55.190 --> 00:12:57.980
Enough so that they never
interfere with us again.

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:01.190
We also want to make
them pay for invading us.

00:13:01.190 --> 00:13:05.530
And you're saying that your taking
of Van is their just reward?

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:10.120
In other words, while an uncompensated
return is impossible,

00:13:10.120 --> 00:13:12.290
if the principality pays reparations,

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:16.500
you would be prepared to comply with
returning the land. Do I have that right?

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:20.670
If the principality pays reparations,
then we will return Van.

00:13:20.670 --> 00:13:23.510
Viewing it in the long run,
it would be a shame to give up land

00:13:23.510 --> 00:13:27.640
that could generate all sorts of wealth,
depending on how it's used,

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:29.350
for a simple one-time payment.

00:13:29.350 --> 00:13:31.770
I don't think it's such a bad decision.

00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:33.930
The empire will have
achieved their just cause

00:13:33.930 --> 00:13:37.520
in seeing that the principality's
territory is returned.

00:13:37.520 --> 00:13:40.150
And as for other non-member nations...

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:44.280
It makes it clear that if
they try anything similar,

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:48.490
they may not lose their territory,
but they will be made to pay reparations.

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:52.080
Leave it to you, Jeanne.
You catch on quickly.

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:55.500
This should earn you some good faith
with non-member nations, too.

00:13:56.920 --> 00:13:59.580
Julius is going to be against this.

00:13:59.580 --> 00:14:01.960
He's the cause of all this,
and I have no pity for him.

00:14:01.960 --> 00:14:06.050
One more thing--please have the
payments be made in imperial coinage.

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:08.300
You're going to drag
my country into this, too?

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:13.220
The empire bears some accountability
for Amidonia's acts of outrage.

00:14:13.220 --> 00:14:15.480
I suppose there's no denying that.

00:14:17.520 --> 00:14:22.570
Tell me, Souma, why did you not
sign on to the Mankind Declaration?

00:14:22.570 --> 00:14:25.490
I hate to say this in front
of Princess Liscia,

00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:27.200
but the reason why the former King Albert

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:31.740
didn't sign the Mankind Declaration...
That is...

00:14:31.740 --> 00:14:34.240
...it's not so much that he
didn't sign it as...

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:37.870
He couldn't decide whether
to sign on to it or not.

00:14:37.870 --> 00:14:39.960
Because he's so indecisive.

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:43.500
Souma, I have to think that you
have a more clear reason

00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:46.630
why you chose not to sign on.

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:51.510
I can't answer her just yet.
Then again, if I lie to her,

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:55.180
it will adversely affect
relations with the empire.

00:14:55.180 --> 00:14:57.100
I hope you will trust me on this,

00:14:57.100 --> 00:15:01.900
but our nation would like
to march in step with yours.

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:04.900
I promise you that as long as
Empress Maria sets forth the ideal

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:08.900
of having all mankind united in response
to the Demon Lord's Domain,

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:12.410
the kingdom is not
the enemy of the empire.

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:17.790
You won't sign on to the Mankind
Declaration, but you say to trust you?

00:15:17.790 --> 00:15:20.540
Our country can't sign on
to the Mankind Declaration,

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:25.170
but we would like to form
a bilateral alliance with the empire.

00:15:25.170 --> 00:15:27.210
One that is secret.

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:30.010
A secret alliance, you say?

00:15:32.090 --> 00:15:35.100
We finally managed to get
our domestic affairs settled.

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:37.680
Starting now, we intend to reform
our military organization,

00:15:37.680 --> 00:15:42.900
and create a system by which we can have
them act under a single, unified will.

00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:48.740
On that point--the empire is currently
sending another detachment

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:51.950
to reinforce the Union
of Eastern Nations, right?

00:15:51.950 --> 00:15:56.080
Yes. They are a collection of
small- and mid-sized nations,

00:15:56.080 --> 00:15:59.830
but most of them are members
of the Mankind Declaration.

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:03.080
As the power behind the treaty,
it's only right that we send forces.

00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:07.670
That's my point. Would you allow
our country to take on that role?

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:10.840
Are you serious?

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:16.260
If the monsters and demons push south,

00:16:16.260 --> 00:16:18.310
they will surely avoid
the Star Dragon Mountain Range,

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:20.810
and end up pushing
either east or west of it.

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:23.940
If they come down the western side,
the empire has them,

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:27.820
and if they come down the eastern side,
the kingdom will deal with them.

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:30.570
That will require some protocols.

00:16:30.570 --> 00:16:34.780
I know. Requests for reinforcements
from the Union of Eastern Nations

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:38.080
will be met by the empire,
head of the Mankind Declaration,

00:16:38.080 --> 00:16:41.790
who will then request that forces
be sent from our country.

00:16:41.790 --> 00:16:44.420
That is the form
I would like this to take.

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:49.920
If it is discovered that the empire
and the kingdom are allied,

00:16:49.920 --> 00:16:52.340
it will make some countries more wary.

00:16:52.340 --> 00:16:55.760
Particularly the Principality of Amidonia,
the Mercenary State Zem,

00:16:55.760 --> 00:16:58.510
and the Republic of Turgis.

00:16:58.510 --> 00:17:01.180
For that reason, as much as possible,

00:17:01.180 --> 00:17:03.810
we do not want it known
that we are working together.

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:07.110
Which is the reason
for the secret alliance.

00:17:07.110 --> 00:17:10.900
For my part, I see no reason
not to accept this proposal.

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:13.990
But how does this benefit you?

00:17:13.990 --> 00:17:18.660
If I had to say, it would be earning
the trust of the empire.

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:21.910
I'm not sure I would call
that much of a benefit.

00:17:21.910 --> 00:17:25.420
Well, when the fate of mankind
rests in the balance,

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:28.080
we can't exactly think in terms
of profits and losses.

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:32.550
And if we <i>don't </i>become involved,
the other nations will look coldly on us.

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:34.220
That makes sense.

00:17:34.220 --> 00:17:37.970
But there's too much distance between
the empire and the kingdom

00:17:37.970 --> 00:17:39.760
for us to communicate quickly.

00:17:39.760 --> 00:17:42.890
I have an idea about that.

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:44.810
Hakuya, bring it in.

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:46.020
Yes, sire.

00:17:46.980 --> 00:17:49.520
I would like to give this to Maria.

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:51.650
A simple receiver?

00:17:53.190 --> 00:17:56.070
If you'll send us
a simple receiver in return,

00:17:56.070 --> 00:17:58.280
we'll be able to contact
each other at any time.

00:17:58.280 --> 00:18:03.120
You could easily converse
with my sister this way, too!

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:06.790
Souma, I shudder in awe
at your inventiveness.

00:18:06.790 --> 00:18:11.210
You're being too dramatic. In the world
I'm from, these were commonplace.

00:18:11.210 --> 00:18:14.630
To think that something
like this is common is just...

00:18:14.630 --> 00:18:20.550
Listen, Souma, would you permit me to
speak of something rash for a moment?

00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:23.010
Huh? I'll allow it.

00:18:23.010 --> 00:18:26.890
Thank you very much.
All right then... Princess Liscia?

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:29.230
Huh? Me?

00:18:29.230 --> 00:18:32.900
What would you say to
returning the throne to Albert?

00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:36.400
And then, you could give
Souma to our country.

00:18:36.400 --> 00:18:37.950
Huh?!

00:18:37.950 --> 00:18:41.120
If he came to us, we would
make him the prime minister,

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:43.080
or any other rank he wants.

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:47.460
In fact, I'd want him to have my
sister and become the emperor!

00:18:47.460 --> 00:18:51.380
Do you even realize
what it is you're saying?!

00:18:51.380 --> 00:18:55.760
Sh-She's right! The princess is
absolutely right! Do you even realize?!

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:59.470
Souma's thinking is ahead of its time.

00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:04.350
I want to see the empire that Souma
and my sister would create.

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:06.350
That's out of the question, of course!

00:19:06.350 --> 00:19:08.520
Souma is someone I...

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:12.650
...is someone our kingdom needs!

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:17.820
Take it easy, Liscia! I'm not
going anywhere! Okay?

00:19:19.860 --> 00:19:22.780
I'm sorry. I lost my head, there.

00:19:22.780 --> 00:19:27.410
Take your hand off your sword!
Aisha, stay!

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:31.000
Y-You're treating me a little harsh,
aren't you, sire?

00:19:32.210 --> 00:19:36.050
I'm sorry, but I can't
accept that proposal.

00:19:36.050 --> 00:19:37.960
For the sake of the kingdom...

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:40.090
...and for the sake
of Liscia and the others.

00:19:40.090 --> 00:19:46.720
I understand. Thank you for
allowing me such a wild proposal.

00:19:46.720 --> 00:19:49.930
Getting back to our
discussion of an alliance,

00:19:49.930 --> 00:19:55.360
a matter as serious as this is something
I cannot decide on my own.

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:57.650
That is what the simple receiver is for.

00:19:57.650 --> 00:20:00.820
It is more than just that;
what would you say to both of us

00:20:00.820 --> 00:20:03.160
sending each other a number
of diplomatic officers?

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:09.750
Oh, I see. That would make working
together much easier. Agreed.

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:12.790
What do you think about assigning
the diplomatic officers the title

00:20:12.790 --> 00:20:15.590
of "Ambassador Extraordinary
and Plenipotentiary,"

00:20:15.590 --> 00:20:19.630
and building "embassies" in both capitals
where they will be stationed?

00:20:19.630 --> 00:20:24.090
That sounds wonderful.
I will start looking into it at once.

00:20:24.090 --> 00:20:28.220
It's getting awfully late.
How about we call it a day?

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:29.770
Yes, of course.

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:43.320
We really have been talking for
quite a while. It's nearly sunrise.

00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:47.240
I feel like we discussed
some things we didn't need to.

00:20:47.240 --> 00:20:52.910
Myself, I'm just glad to have
found a friend I can count on.

00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:57.210
I have something to say
to my good friend from the east.

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:59.920
What is it, good friend from the west?

00:20:59.920 --> 00:21:04.340
The being within the Demon Lord's Realm,
which we call the Demon Lord...

00:21:06.260 --> 00:21:08.890
...we don't know the demons' language,

00:21:08.890 --> 00:21:12.560
but they seem to say
one word rather often.

00:21:12.560 --> 00:21:19.320
My country's researchers surmise
that it may be the Demon Lord's name.

00:21:19.320 --> 00:21:21.570
It being...

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:23.240
..."Divalroi."

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:27.160
Divalroi? The Demon Lord Divalroi?

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:29.240
Yes.

00:21:29.240 --> 00:21:31.490
The Demon Lord Divalroi...

00:21:31.490 --> 00:21:34.540
The Demon Lord... Divalroi...

00:21:34.540 --> 00:21:37.000
The Demon Lord...

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:41.920
Huh? What is this? I remember
hearing this somewhere before.

00:21:41.920 --> 00:21:48.300
Is it déjà vu? No, that's not it.
I remember hearing it, from somewhere...

00:21:50.600 --> 00:21:51.770
Souma!

00:21:53.060 --> 00:21:57.900
Serina, show Jeanne to her guest room.

00:22:02.280 --> 00:22:06.110
I'm all right. I can sleep
in the bed in my office.

00:22:06.110 --> 00:22:09.120
No, you're going to sleep in a proper bed.

00:22:12.870 --> 00:22:14.620
I don't know what's behind it,

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:17.870
but when you're exhausted,
at least, let me pamper you.

00:22:17.870 --> 00:22:20.750
Sorry. Thanks.

00:22:21.960 --> 00:22:23.760
You're welcome.

00:22:35.020 --> 00:22:39.060
<i>"What are we supposed to choose?"</i>

00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:44.320
<i>Our voices imploring the future are hoarse</i>

00:22:44.320 --> 00:22:50.410
<i>We've become so afraid</i>
<i>of what we could lose</i>

00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:55.370
<i>that we're just frozen in place</i>

00:22:55.370 --> 00:22:59.830
<i>How many times have we made mistakes</i>

00:22:59.830 --> 00:23:05.800
<i>because we wanted to check our "answers"?</i>

00:23:05.800 --> 00:23:13.140
<i>Before we knew it we were in love,</i>
<i>we had fallen in love</i>

00:23:13.140 --> 00:23:17.390
<i>I'll hold fast to you</i>
<i>in the times we're in</i>

00:23:17.390 --> 00:23:23.190
<i>We who set alight</i>
<i>our finite lives to fight</i>

00:23:23.190 --> 00:23:28.450
<i>are noble and beautiful above all</i>

00:23:28.450 --> 00:23:32.410
<i>As long as we create</i>
<i>as many bright tomorrows</i>

00:23:32.410 --> 00:23:37.750
<i>as the indelible wounds we suffer,</i>

00:23:37.750 --> 00:23:46.800
<i>we can be proud of all</i>
<i>we've woven together</i>
